## Deliverable
Implemented the private Gherkin source index in `src/extract/gherkin.ts`. No commit.

The index:
- splits LF/CRLF source into physical one-based lines exactly once;
- uses `GherkinDocument.comments[*].location.line` from the official parser as the only comment-line authority;
- indexes Feature, Background, Scenario, Examples, Rule, and Rule-child description owners from the official AST;
- aligns every AST description entry monotonically and by exact text;
- skips only parser-identified comment lines and whitespace-only physical lines;
- carries `{ text, line }` entries into Feature/Scenario description parsing;
- uses the first located nonblank prose line for Rule and `@example-space` description refusals;
- returns one `extract/gherkin-syntax` finding and no Specs/Packs on a nonblank mismatch or EOF;
- retains language-header lookup in the same physical source index, avoiding a second line split.

No Gherkin structure is inferred from raw source. Valid metadata, identity-tag locations, graph data, and contract data are unchanged.

