## Failure-path QA: injected official-AST/source divergence
A temporary esbuild stdin seam bundled the finalized extractor without changing the worktree. The seam ran the official parser first, then changed only the returned Feature description before source indexing.

Two assertions were exercised:
- nonblank mismatch: AST `outcom` versus physical `outcome`;
- EOF: append one AST-only prose entry.

For each result the probe asserted exactly one finding, `extract/gherkin-syntax`, zero Specs, and zero Packs. Observed:

```
{"file":"alignment-mismatch.sdp.gherkin","specs":0,"packs":0,"findings":1,"validatorId":"extract/gherkin-syntax","line":3}
{"file":"alignment-eof.sdp.gherkin","specs":0,"packs":0,"findings":1,"validatorId":"extract/gherkin-syntax","line":4}
```

The temporary bundle was removed. No test-only hook or generated file remains in the worktree.

